# Decisions Log — nab-anomaly-detector
# Rule 3: each entry is a reconciliation or design decision.

## 2026-08-06 — Bootstrap (step-000)
- Decision: ledger.json commit_sha for step-000 is null because a commit cannot embed its own SHA. Will be patched in the next run (same approach as vuln-triage-ai step-000).
- Decision: 21-step plan frozen per Rule 1. Plan covers Phases 10-16 (bootstrap through publish).
- Decision: No API keys needed for this project (pure Python, public data). No human gate for credentials.
- Decision: NAB dataset will be downloaded via git clone or direct download in step-001, not bundled in the repo (too large).
- Decision: requirements.txt starts minimal (pytest only); dependencies added as detectors are built (pandas, scikit-learn, numpy, streamlit).

2026-08-07 step-001: Downloaded NAB dataset (58 CSVs + 2 label files) via src/download_nab.py. Data is gitignored; CI downloads fresh. 10 new tests verify CSV format, label integrity, and dataset completeness. WALKTHROUGH.md Section 5 documents the 7 categories, format, and label structure. Chose zip-extract method over per-file urllib (60x faster). Patched step-000 commit_sha to bfb3082.
